  ],
  "description": "redundancy.v1 §2.2: a contract's uses and each resource's resolved annotations (core §9.3, any order), and whether the deployment's tokenless set names the interface -> its declaration. contract.uses lists profile ids as <name>.v<major>; contract.resources[].annotations is the resource's merged annotations. expect.declaration is one of: \"not_governed\" (uses lists no redundancy.v1 and no resource carries redundancy.election; or uses lists another major of redundancy and not v1, that major's text then governing its keys); \"governed\", with election, \"claim\" or \"external\": the one election every resource resolves to, a resource carrying none read as claim, an interface with no resource claim; or \"invalid\", with reasons, in this order, each checked alone: not_used (a resource carries redundancy.election, and uses names no major of redundancy: core E020's), value (a resource's redundancy.election is not the string claim or external), disagrees (two resources resolve to two elections, each valid, one carrying none read as claim; a resource found value takes no part), tokenless (governed, and the tokenless set names the interface). Another redundancy.<key> makes nothing invalid (it is W105's), and annotations on requirements are not read."
